    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "RAPID-CA is a statewide survey that seeks to uplift the voices of families with young children across California and provide policymakers with timely, actionable data about the needs and priorities of those families. As part of my field project with the POLS program, I supported the RAPID-CA team's work by identifying gaps in survey representation (by geography, race, language, and citizenship status) and created a landscape analysis of early childhood organizations that could support RAPID-CA's outreach efforts across the state. I conducted a demographic analysis of RAPID-CA's respondents to identify underrepresented groups, then researched organizations that serve families with young children who reflect the diversity of California. These artifacts are a landscape analysis of early childhood organizations in California as well as a written brief synthesizing key findings and recommendations for the RAPID-CA team.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Daugherty, K. (2024). Analyzing the Landscape of Early Childhood Organizations in California . Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/nz684km7134. https://doi.org/10.25740/nz684km7134.",
